dsh-pavement-design-methods
============================

A STUDY AID and CRITICAL COMMENTARY derived from the Chinese monograph
《路面设计原理与方法》(第 4 版), published by 人民交通出版社.

What this package is:

  * a structured paraphrase of the book's arguments, written in our own words, with page
    references so a reader can check every claim against the printed book;
  * an ERRATA REGISTER: roughly a hundred transcription defects, internal contradictions and
    numbering faults found while distilling the book are documented card by card, each with the
    page and, where possible, a recomputation. This register is the package's own contribution;
  * a boundary statement: the book's two design chapters contain no reproducible worked example,
    and its only complete hand calculation ends with a wrong verdict. The package says so.

What this package is NOT:

  * it is not the book, and cannot substitute for it;
  * it contains no verbatim passages. An automated audit against two source transcriptions found a
    longest shared run of zero characters across all 63 cards; the few ten-character matches that
    remain are chapter titles, the book title, and parameter-name pairs used as table labels, all
    registered as structural exemptions;
  * all formulas are marked unchecked against the printed page, and all numbers are marked as
    transcription values.

The book's chapter 9 (airport pavements) and the tail of chapter 8 were replaced by unrelated
textbook content during transcription. This package declares them lost and does not invent them.

Copyright in the underlying book remains with its authors and publisher.

